  "body": "We have tests at https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/8158699f81fb068af4fb8f70661388b1fdb88813/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/environment-changes/iframed.sub.html#L39-L45 that currently appear to expect a load event (c.f. https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues/12656). https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/environment-changes/viewport-change.html shows that all browsers pass the test as currently written. This implies that the browsers get the fetch response for the new image, see that it is corrupt, fire a load event (???), and upgrade the pending request to the current one so that currentSrc returns the new broken.png URL. [The specification](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#reacting-to-environment-changes) says in step 14.5 to \"let pending request be null and abort these steps\".\r\n\r\ncc @zcorpan ",
